{"name":"UCLA Blue","hex":"#536895","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"UCLA Bruins","blocks":[{"text":"The UCLA Bruins are the athletic teams that represent the University of California, Los Angeles. The Bruin men's and women's teams participate in NCAA Division I as part of the Big Ten Conference and the Mountain Pacific Sports Federation (MPSF). For football, they are in the Football Bowl Subdivision of Division I. UCLA is second to only Stanford University as the school with the most NCAA team championships at 127 NCAA team championships. UCLA offers 11 varsity sports programs for men and 14 for women."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/UCLA_Bruins_primary_logo.svg/330px-UCLA_Bruins_primary_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UCLA_Bruins","wikidata":"Q1753811"},{"title":"University of California, Los Angeles","blocks":[{"text":"The University of California, Los Angeles (UCLA) is a public land-grant research university in the Westwood neighborhood of Los Angeles, California, United States. Its academic roots were established in 1881 as the southern branch of the California State Normal School, which is now San José State University. The campus was transferred to the University of California to become its southern branch in 1919, making it the second-oldest of the 10-campus University of California system after the University of California, Berkeley. It officially became independent from Berkeley on June 14, 1951, and set the precedent to further strip CAL's administrative oversight over University of California, Davis, University of California, Riverside, University of California, San Diego, and University of California, San Francisco."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/The_University_of_California_UCLA.svg/330px-The_University_of_California_UCLA.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_California%2C_Los_Angeles","wikidata":"Q174710"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Ucla_wordmrk_2017.png/500px-Ucla_wordmrk_2017.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Ucla_wordmrk_2017.png/500px-Ucla_wordmrk_2017.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUcla_wordmrk_2017.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/UCLA_out_in_left_field_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-UCLA_out_in_left_field_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/UCLA_out_in_left_field_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-UCLA_out_in_left_field_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/UCLA_out_in_left_field_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-UCLA_out_in_left_field_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Bruins baseball team gathering in the outfield at Jackie Robinson Stadium in 2007","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUCLA_out_in_left_field_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/PauleyPavilion1202026.png/500px-PauleyPavilion1202026.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/PauleyPavilion1202026.png/1280px-PauleyPavilion1202026.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/PauleyPavilion1202026.png/500px-PauleyPavilion1202026.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"#4 Purdue Boilermakers vs. UCLA, January 20th, 2026. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APauleyPavilion1202026.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/ROSEBOWLUCLAFRONT1042025.png/500px-ROSEBOWLUCLAFRONT1042025.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/ROSEBOWLUCLAFRONT1042025.png/1280px-ROSEBOWLUCLAFRONT1042025.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo